  "notes": [
   "Parts unchanged from step 1.",
   "Pushbutton straddles the centre gap in columns 10 and 12. The image shows both wires on the same half of the board, but the catalogue treats 1.l/1.r as one side and 2.l/2.r as the other. So the pin-2 wire goes to side 1 (top half, column 10) and the GND wire to side 2 (bottom half, column 12). This puts the switch between pin 2 and GND, as the schematic shows.",
   "Which Uno GND header the black wire uses is not distinguishable in the image. GND.1 is assumed, and all Uno GND pins are the same net.",
   "No resistor: pin 2 uses the internal pull-up (INPUT_PULLUP) and pin 13 uses the onboard LED, so there is no external LED.",
   "The USB cable links the Uno to the computer for serial and power. The computer is not modelled, and the cable has no ports in the catalogue, so the edge is port-less."
  ]
 },
